  For one thing, possessing good social skills helps students cooperate smoothly with teammates in group tasks. They can exchange ideas and settle disagreements properly,
making group projects easier to complete. For another, good social skills allow students to build wider social networks. These connections can offer valuable information about 
internships and future career chances.
  From my perspective, students should develop social skills for their future career. Only in this way can students gain advantages in job hunting.



